gts7xlwifi: DRAM below the kernel's window becomes VM memory (port of UniXNU 8f5a4e9 to xnu-10063)

Upstream's profiles/os/macos-27.3-26C5035r/patches/xnu-12377/window-outside-memory-adoption.patch, rewritten for the
iPadOS 17.7.11 kernel (xnu-10063.141.1, BCM2837 config: no PPL, no KTRR/CTRR, no ARM_LARGE_MEMORY). The kernel window
starts at 0x10AD00000 (firmware-t970 "XNU window"), so the HLOS DRAM below it that the firmware's map keeps reserved
is listed in /chosen/darwinboot-memory-outside by board.toml (static: the firmware's DarwinBoot has no outside table)
and adopted page by page once the VM runs. Opt-in: memory-outside=1; memory-outside-floor=ADDR adopts only what lies at or above ADDR. See docs/ram-outside-window.md.

Differences from upstream: vm_page_create(pn, pn + 1) instead of vm_page_create_canonical() (10063 has no page radix
tree; a vm_page outside the linear array keeps its page number itself, as for ml_static_mfree); the aperture VA lies a
twig-rounded span below LOW_GLOBAL_BASE_ADDRESS - 4 GiB, inside pmap_virtual_region 3, which kmem_init reserves on this
config (upstream's ROUND_L1 is 64 GiB with 16 KiB pages and would leave that region); default off.
Apply after t970-dram-holes.patch and t970-three-clusters.patch (generated against the fully patched main1 tree).

